---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Get help with mdbase, mdbase Connect, and the mdbase plugin for ChatGPT, Claude, and other MCP clients."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">Where to get help with mdbase, Connect, and connected applications.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button button--primary" href="mailto:callum@mdbase.dev"
        >Email support</a
      >
      <a class="button" href="https://status.mdbase.dev">Service status</a>
    </div>
  </header>
  <article class="legal">

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:callum@mdbase.dev">callum@mdbase.dev</a> for help with
      your account, a connected application, or anything on this page. Include
      the application you were using, what you expected, and what happened.
      Never send passwords, encryption passwords, recovery keys, recovery
      codes, or collection contents.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report bugs and feature requests in the relevant repository in the
      <a href="https://github.com/mdbase-dev">mdbase GitHub organization</a>.
      Report security issues as described on the <a href="/security/">security page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>ChatGPT, Claude, and other MCP clients</h2>
    <p>
      The mdbase plugin and connector use the MCP endpoint <code>https://mcp.mdbase.dev/mcp</code>.
      Each collection is approved separately, with its own operations.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>A collection is missing.</strong> Ask the assistant to connect
        another collection, then approve it at the link it gives you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Writes are refused.</strong> The collection was approved for
        reading only. Ask the assistant to reconnect it and approve write
        access.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Operations fail or time out.</strong> A Private collection, or
        one with sync off, is reachable only while one of your devices that
        holds it is online, such as a computer running the desktop app. Cloud
        copy collections don’t depend on your devices. Check
        <a href="https://status.mdbase.dev">service status</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Manage or revoke access</h2>
    <p>
      Review connected applications, collections, and devices in
      <a href="https://editor.mdbase.dev/connect">Connect</a>. Revoking an
      application's access takes effect on its next request. To be sure an
      assistant can no longer reach a collection, revoke its access in Connect
      rather than only removing the plugin or connector from the assistant.
    </p>

    <h2>Private collections</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>You forgot your encryption password.</strong> Enter your
        recovery key instead, then set a new password. mdbase can’t reset the
        password or recover the key for you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A new device can’t open a Private collection.</strong> Sign in,
        then enter your encryption password or recovery key. In strict mode,
        approve the device from one you already have and check that both show
        the same six-digit code.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Accounts and data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/account-deletion/">Delete a Connect account</a></li>
      <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/terms/">Terms</a></li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
